        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the function returning -EIO when no best clock sample value was found, even though there were candidate values available. This behavior was inappropriate as it prevented the eMMC from functioning correctly. The intended behavior was to use the first candidate value when no best value could be determined, allowing the system to continue operating instead of failing with an error.

